WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.360
At the start of 2025, I joined&nbsp;
Mode as their Chief Design Officer.&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.880
My first task? Reimagining the company's brand.
But where do you begin?&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.920
How do you position your brand&nbsp;
to stand out from competitors?&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.120
Why risk changing something that already works?
And how can a rebrand transform a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.400
business and shape its future products?
Hello, I'm Matthew Encina. In this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.720
I’ll walk you through the process of&nbsp;
building a brand, from start to finish.&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.920
Thanks to Shopify for sponsoring this video.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.000
Before we begin, I’ll give a&nbsp;
little context on how we got here.&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.120
The story of Mode begins when our founder&nbsp;
Jaicob discovers mechanical keyboards while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.520
working as a software engineer. What&nbsp;
starts as a hobby—building his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.480
custom keyboard—evolves into a quest&nbsp;
for the perfect typing experience.&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.600
This obsession sparks ideas that lead to&nbsp;
late-night designing, which becomes Mode's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:02.000
first product: a batch of 50 keyboards.
No outside investments. No crowdfunding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.880
No guarantee of success.
The keyboard isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.880
perfect—first attempts rarely are—but 50&nbsp;
incredible humans take a chance on Mode.&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.200
Since then, Mode has grown steadily, reinvesting&nbsp;
in better keyboards with each production run.&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:23.680
Now, five years later, it has transformed from a&nbsp;
side project into a company with a clear vision:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:29.120
Mode isn't just about keyboards—it's about&nbsp;
how thoughtful design transforms everyday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:35.040
experiences. This vision comes to life through&nbsp;
our small, dedicated remote team across Boston,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.120
San Francisco, and Los Angeles.
That’s where I come in.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.800
As a creative professional in design, advertising,&nbsp;
and branding since 2003, I've collaborated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.840
some of the biggest brands in the world.
My path takes an unexpected turn when my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.560
own keyboard obsession leads me to&nbsp;
explore industrial product design.&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.920
In 2022, I discover Mode and instantly&nbsp;
connect with their design aesthetic.&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.160
As a DIY project, I create an&nbsp;
oak accent piece for their Sonnet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.400
keyboard—I love how wood brings warmth to&nbsp;
tech peripherals. This becomes an official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:13.040
Mode product and leads to a bigger project:&nbsp;
designing an entire keyboard from scratch.&nbsp;

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.880
These successes, combined with my&nbsp;
experience, pave the way for me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:23.600
to join Mode as Chief Design Officer in 2025,&nbsp;
where I now lead the brand and product vision.&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.480
It's a huge responsibility, but&nbsp;
I'm thrilled by what’s next.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.120
You might be wondering: if a company&nbsp;
is doing well, why change anything?&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.600
Over the last five years, we’ve grown and&nbsp;
developed clearer opinions on what we want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:43.360
Mode to be, what values drive our product&nbsp;
design, and how we want to do business.&nbsp;

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.400
So we want to update the brand to reflect that.
The questions on our minds are:&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.040
Where have we been in the last five years,&nbsp;
and what’s our vision for Mode in the future?&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.360
How might we position our brand and&nbsp;
products to be distinct in the marketplace?&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.440
What‘s worth keeping and what needs&nbsp;
to change for our business to grow?&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.000
And this is where the branding process comes in.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.400
While most people associate a brand&nbsp;
with its logo, colors, and typefaces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.520
it's so much more than that.
"A brand is a person's gut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.120
feeling about a product, service, or company."
Every touchpoint and interaction shapes how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.560
customers perceive the brand.
A strong brand:&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.480
Has an outstanding reputation
Is perceived as valuable&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.880
Stands out from competitors
Forms genuine connections with customers&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.160
Our branding process examines all aspects&nbsp;
of our business—positioning, product,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:38.800
culture, and customers—to determine what&nbsp;
changes will help us achieve our goals.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.320
This process takes several weeks and&nbsp;
follows the Double Diamond framework.&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:50.240
A brand refresh is no easy task, and while&nbsp;
I'm up for the challenge, it's always good to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:56.640
have an extra creative mind to collaborate with.
This is Ben Burns, an old co-worker and friend.&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.120
He's a well-rounded creative with excellent&nbsp;
taste. As the former Digital Director at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.160
Blind and Chief Operating Officer at The&nbsp;
Futur, we collaborated on numerous client&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.640
projects and digital products together.
When Ben became available for design work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.280
I jumped at the chance to bring him on&nbsp;
board to facilitate our branding process.&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.080
With Ben's involvement, I can focus on crafting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.240
the brand vision while he provides&nbsp;
an objective outside perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:28.240
serving as both a sounding board for ideas&nbsp;
and a skilled hand in bringing them to life.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.280
First, we begin with the Discover Phase. We&nbsp;
expand our understanding of the brand vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:39.600
business goals, and challenges while gathering&nbsp;
data on products, customers, and the market.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.760
We kick off our Discovery process&nbsp;
by getting the team together at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:50.480
my LA studio. The crew includes Jaicob (our&nbsp;
CEO), Xris (our Head of Marketing), myself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.440
and Ben, who guides us through the session.
Before jumping into the brand exercises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:01.120
we took some time to align on our bigger&nbsp;
company goals. Here's what rose to the top:&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:05.920
Establish a distinct brand voice with&nbsp;
a clear identity and point of view.&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.960
deepen our understanding of current customers&nbsp;
while identifying and planning for new ones.&nbsp;

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:15.920
Update and refine our product catalog to better&nbsp;
serve our customers and reflect our brand.&nbsp;

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:21.200
And, increase revenue over the next 5 years&nbsp;
to invest in more challenging projects.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.560
Before our meetup, we spend weeks gathering&nbsp;
research and data. We analyze website traffic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:32.000
sales data, and conduct customer surveys&nbsp;
within the keyboard community to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.560
trends and preferences. We also&nbsp;
do in-depth video interviews with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.680
specific community members to learn&nbsp;
why they buy or pass on our products.&nbsp;

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:46.480
These insights inform our in-person&nbsp;
user exercises, where we identify and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.360
segment our current and future customer&nbsp;
base to better understand who we serve.&nbsp;

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:56.880
We know our current customers–many by name– so&nbsp;
we focus our exercises on how we can attract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:03.280
new ones. Our research helps us create detailed&nbsp;
user personas with names and stories that reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.640
what matters to these potential customers.
We then map how each customer type interacts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.240
with our brand from discovery to purchase,&nbsp;
noting what influences their decisions and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.840
what holds them back. This helps&nbsp;
us spot hurdles we need to address.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:21.600
There were many customers we considered, but here&nbsp;
are two examples of personas and their journeys:&nbsp;

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:28.000
First is Tim, an experienced UX Design Manager in&nbsp;
Austin, Texas. He extensively researches products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:34.240
before purchasing. Tim values quality, community,&nbsp;
and knowing the people behind the brands. As a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.200
hobby enthusiast, he’d likely enjoy building&nbsp;
our keyboard kits. For customers like Tim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:45.280
we need detailed product information available and&nbsp;
to make the community around our brand visible.&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.560
Then there's Jay, a young software engineer&nbsp;
in San Francisco, California who's seeking a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.280
workspace upgrade. Jay is busy, so he doesn’t&nbsp;
want to spend a lot of time trying to find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:00.960
better keyboard. He relies on influencer&nbsp;
and publication recommendations. For him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:07.680
we need a simple purchase process with clear&nbsp;
guidance and the option for ready-to-use products.&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.560
Looking at different user types gives us a&nbsp;
valuable perspective on improving our products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:20.000
and customer experience. With these insights, we&nbsp;
now turn our focus inward to examine our brand.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.080
In the next series of exercises, we examine our&nbsp;
brand through multiple lenses: values and beliefs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.000
features and benefits, voice&nbsp;
and tone, and look and feel.&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.440
Using focused prompts, our&nbsp;
team brainstorms freely.&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.560
We group similar ideas and prioritize&nbsp;
what resonates most deeply. The word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.960
clusters reveal clear themes that shape&nbsp;
our brand's characteristics. These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.720
attributes we currently embody and ideals we&nbsp;
will continue to pursue as we grow the brand.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.280
Using the brand attributes defined from&nbsp;
our prompts, we analyze our positioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:57.200
in the competitive landscape.
Positioning is the space a brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.920
occupies in the hearts and minds of&nbsp;
customers, relative to competitors.&nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:07.920
For our exercise, we create an X&amp;Y map with&nbsp;
opposing brand qualities. We plot both our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:13.280
competitors and brands from other industries&nbsp;
to visualize where we stand in the market.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:19.280
For our voice, we ask: Are we understated&nbsp;
or outspoken? Are we an opaque company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.360
or more transparent and human?
For our aesthetic: Are we warm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:29.600
and inviting or stark and industrial? Are&nbsp;
we highly curated or raw and unedited?&nbsp;

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.360
Are our products expensive,&nbsp;
or are they budget options?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:39.840
Are they considered premium or the standard?
What we find is eye-opening and sparks a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:45.840
of discussion. In some areas, we are swimming&nbsp;
in a crowded pool without much to set us apart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.960
This realization pushes us to ask important&nbsp;
questions: How can we carve out our own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.680
unique space? What do we need to change to&nbsp;
create distinction from our competitors?&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:01.760
This helps us refine our brand positioning as&nbsp;
we wrap up our work for the Discovery Phase.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:05.680
Moving into the Define phase, we&nbsp;
synthesize everything we learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.400
during Discovery to clarify our design challenge.&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.400
The research and discussions helped us&nbsp;
understand our business better and where we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:20.160
fit in the market. These insights come together&nbsp;
during our LA meeting, but become even clearer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:26.400
as we reflect on them over the following weeks.
What emerges is a clear vision for Mode's future.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:32.840
We start seeing patterns and themes that resonate&nbsp;
with everyone on the team. Ideas like "Warm Tech"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:39.600
- making technology feel more human and inviting.&nbsp;
"Creating joy in everyday experiences" - because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.400
keyboards shouldn't just be functional, they&nbsp;
should bring delight. And "making products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:51.200
that deserve to exist" - focusing on quality and&nbsp;
innovation rather than just adding to the noise.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:56.560
But having a vision isn't enough. We have to make&nbsp;
some tough decisions about our product lineup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.560 --> 00:10:01.600
This means taking a hard look at our current&nbsp;
offerings and being honest about what needs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:07.280
change. As a result, we're discontinuing certain&nbsp;
products to sharpen our focus on better ones.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:13.680
We also know our visual identity, messaging, and&nbsp;
website need a complete overhaul to better serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:19.440
our customers and reflect our new direction.
In this Define Phase, we have a clear set of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.200
Design Challenges to address&nbsp;
in the rest of the process:&nbsp;

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.880
How might we create products that&nbsp;
feel thoughtfully crafted rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.760
than mass-produced—objects that bring&nbsp;
joy and warmth to people's spaces?&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.640
How might we design a brand identity&nbsp;
that feels high-end and curated while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:41.440
still feeling humble and human?
How might we design a website&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:47.520
that seamlessly guides both newcomers and&nbsp;
experienced enthusiasts through their journey?

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:51.920
We want the shopping experience to be&nbsp;
simple and smooth, so we use Shopify,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.960
the sponsor of this video.
Shopify is a powerful set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:11:00.000
of tools that helps you start and manage&nbsp;
your business, whether online or in-person.&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.280
When Mode started its keyboard business&nbsp;
in 2019, managing an e-commerce operation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:09.600
while developing its first product&nbsp;
felt overwhelming. Thanks to Shopify,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.400
setting up a store was simple, letting Mode&nbsp;
focus on delivering their first product.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.840
As Mode grew, maintaining enough capital to&nbsp;
fund orders became crucial for operations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:25.200
Shopify Capital provides flexible funding that&nbsp;
you can repay as you sell, accessible at every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:30.480
stage of growth, right from your dashboard.
This enables businesses like ours to seize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.920
opportunities by improving cash&nbsp;
flow—especially when investing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:38.000
in inventory to maintain steady sales.
Shopify is there for you when you’re just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:43.120
starting out, and grows with your business.&nbsp;
It has apps to build and customize your store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:48.160
and ways to connect and sell natively on social&nbsp;
platforms to meet your customers where they are.&nbsp;

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:55.120
Thanks to Shopify for sponsoring this video.&nbsp;
Go to shopify.com/matthewencina to learn more.&nbsp;

00:11:55.120 --> 00:12:00.640
Now that we have our direction, we move into&nbsp;
expansive exploration in the Develop Phase,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.760
exploring ideas for the new brand and&nbsp;
creating solutions that address our goals.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:10.000
We begin with stylescapes, which&nbsp;
are carefully curated mood boards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:15.840
This is a process Ben and I use to transform&nbsp;
abstract ideas into concrete visuals, allowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:21.440
us to explore different design directions quickly&nbsp;
before we invest time in custom design work.&nbsp;

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:27.120
Drawing from our Discovery and Define phases, we&nbsp;
identify key themes that shape each direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:32.400
We gather visual references that match these&nbsp;
themes, adjust them to create visual harmony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:37.280
and arrange them on a wide layout.
Stylescapes provide a preview of how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.920
brand looks across different touchpoints,&nbsp;
from packaging to digital screens.&nbsp;

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.680
We develop three distinct directions&nbsp;
to present to the Mode team:&nbsp;

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:51.600
First, there’s "Serious Fun"&nbsp;
- clean, curated, and colorful&nbsp;

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:58.880
Next, "Crafted Narrative" - inspired by&nbsp;
editorial design with rich, contrasting colors&nbsp;

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:05.680
Lastly, "Bits of Joy" - bright and fun, with&nbsp;
a modern take at nostalgic lo-fi graphics&nbsp;

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.160
During the presentation, we look for what&nbsp;
resonates with the team and how well each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:15.600
direction matches our defined brand values.&nbsp;
The second direction proves to be most popular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:19.440
particularly for its dark green&nbsp;
palette and typography choices.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.320
The team also likes elements&nbsp;
from the other directions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:27.360
including the bitmap typefaces from "Bits of&nbsp;
Joy" and illustrations from "Serious Fun."&nbsp;

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.680
Based on this feedback, we combine the best&nbsp;
elements to create our final stylescape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:36.880
"The Story of Craft." This direction&nbsp;
features editorial-inspired typography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:42.240
hand-drawn elements, and maker marks that&nbsp;
showcase our craftsmanship. Rich colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:47.680
warm tones, and imagery highlight&nbsp;
how our products bring joy to spaces.&nbsp;

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:53.360
This stylescape serves as our foundation&nbsp;
for developing the complete visual identity.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:14:00.000
The first design project we take on is the&nbsp;
website. It’s the largest asset we need to create,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.400
but also has the most opportunities to&nbsp;
figure out many aspects of the brand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:10.000
like typography, imagery, and colors. The goal&nbsp;
is to create an experience that reflects our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:15.600
new brand and feels intuitive, whether you're&nbsp;
a first-time visitor or a keyboard enthusiast.&nbsp;

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.840
First, we create a sitemap, a bird's&nbsp;
eye view of every page on the website.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:24.320
It's challenging to think through, but it&nbsp;
allows us to plan for all the various paths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:29.200
a user can take on our site. This process&nbsp;
allows us to test different user journeys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.640
ensuring customers can easily&nbsp;
find what they're looking for.&nbsp;

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.920
Next, we create two key pages using placeholder&nbsp;
content. This gives us a sense of the overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:45.520
aesthetic and the components we need, like menus,&nbsp;
typography styles, buttons, galleries, and more.&nbsp;

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:48.880
Once we’re happy with these two&nbsp;
pages, it takes us a few weeks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:54.320
create and refine the rest of the website.
Typography plays a big part of any brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.320 --> 00:15:00.160
identity. In our stylescapes, we determine that we&nbsp;
want to use a combination of serif and sans-serif,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:06.320
for our header and body copy, and selective use&nbsp;
of bitmap-style typefaces as a fun nod to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:11.280
history of computing and mechanical keyboards.
We can test different typeface combinations in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:16.000
a type specimen, and look at them in context&nbsp;
on our sample webpages. We finally choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:22.720
to add a monospace font for technical copy to&nbsp;
highlight the engineering aspects of our work.

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:27.200
Next is choosing our colors for the&nbsp;
brand, which is more complex than you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:31.840
might think. We need a palette that works&nbsp;
across all of our brand collateral - from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:37.120
physical packaging to our website on screen.
For the main color, we all fell in love with this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:43.440
deep green. It’s bold yet calming because of its&nbsp;
ties to nature. To support this, we choose a set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:49.280
of secondary colors that can be used as accents.
Ben and I spend multiple sessions reviewing color&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:54.320
swatches and combinations. This is one of the&nbsp;
most intense parts of the process because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.320 --> 00:16:00.880
impacts so many aspects of the brand and&nbsp;
business. It’s so important to get right.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:06.240
Photography plays a crucial role in bringing&nbsp;
our brand to life. I pull together reference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:11.760
images that best capture these qualities and&nbsp;
spend time thinking about the key principles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:15.600
for our photography style.
Strong directional lighting&nbsp;

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:21.920
Warm and natural tones with subtle film grain
Scenes that feel lived-in but not messy&nbsp;

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.680
People featured in a way that&nbsp;
doesn't detract from the product&nbsp;

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.720
These rules and references should&nbsp;
provide enough guidance for our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:33.840
team to capture photos and videos&nbsp;
that fit our new brand direction.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.920
Crafting our brand voice is another&nbsp;
challenging task. We want to sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:44.080
professional but not corporate, friendly but&nbsp;
not fake - a difficult balance to strike. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:49.920
keyboard world is full of technical jargon,&nbsp;
so we make a conscious effort to use clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:55.120
simple language that anyone can understand.
Using a Notion document, we collaborate to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.120 --> 00:17:00.000
write and refine our core messages, making&nbsp;
sure our word choices feel authentic to who we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:07.840
are. This means avoiding marketing buzzwords and&nbsp;
focusing on honest, straightforward communication.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:13.440
With the key aspects of our brand identity&nbsp;
developed, I shift my focus onto the product.&nbsp;

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:19.280
Our new brand concept of "Warm Tech" has become&nbsp;
the north star of our product design. While most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:24.240
tech feels cold and manufactured, we want&nbsp;
our products to feel crafted and human.&nbsp;

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:28.800
As one customer tells us during interviews,&nbsp;
"a nice keyboard can be like a piece of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:33.920
furniture that ties the room together."
This insight deeply resonates with our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:39.120
vision and becomes a guiding principle that&nbsp;
shapes our product design. Like a well-chosen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:44.800
piece of furniture transforms a room, a carefully&nbsp;
crafted keyboard should elevate your workspace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:50.480
while bringing joy to your everyday experience.
I start by exploring different forms, colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.680
materials, and finishes we&nbsp;
can use on our products.&nbsp;

00:17:53.680 --> 00:18:01.120
Then I take these as inspiration to begin the&nbsp;
lengthy process of designing our next keyboard.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.240
We are now in the final phase&nbsp;
of the rebranding process:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:10.800
Deliver. We refine our best concepts into a clear&nbsp;
brand strategy and refreshed identity system.&nbsp;

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:15.840
The biggest challenge in this phase is getting&nbsp;
all the small details right. While reaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:23.200
90% completion is relatively straightforward,&nbsp;
the final 10% takes the most time and effort.&nbsp;

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:29.120
We're four months into the process, and the more&nbsp;
we make, the more we learn. As we know better, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:35.280
iterate on our earliest work to ensure everything&nbsp;
is cohesive and drives us toward our goals.&nbsp;

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:39.760
The delivery phase will take months to roll&nbsp;
out fully, and we’ll continue to work on it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:44.400
beyond this video. For now, let me show&nbsp;
you what we've accomplished so far.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:54.800
First, we've finalized our brand identity&nbsp;
guidelines. This gives us a clear framework&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.800 --> 00:19:01.200
for how we present ourselves to the world.
Starting with the logo usage: We kept our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:06.320
existing logo because it works well, and we’ve&nbsp;
built brand equity around it. It wasn’t something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:11.840
I felt needed changing so we focused on&nbsp;
slight refinements, and detailed usage.&nbsp;

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:17.600
We’ve developed a cohesive visual language&nbsp;
with carefully chosen typography, colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:25.440
and imagery. One aspect that has grown since&nbsp;
our stylescape exploration is the lo-fi bitmap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:31.520
imagery, inspired by retro computing, tapping into&nbsp;
the history of mechanical keyboards. We’re calling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:36.800
this the “alter-ego” of our brand. This drives&nbsp;
the language of our custom-made iconography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:43.360
logo variant, and is a fun way to process photos.
To shape how our brand speaks, we establish clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:48.480
language rules that create a distinctive&nbsp;
voice and tone that feels human, confident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:54.160
and helpful. This includes messaging samples&nbsp;
we can use on the website and in marketing.&nbsp;

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.240
We also have a separate guide of brand&nbsp;
expressions. A showcase of our brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:02.560
across physical and digital platforms&nbsp;
to explore different ways it can look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:08.080
and feel. These aren’t meant to be final&nbsp;
products, but rather are thought-starters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:15.120
to draw from when creating assets for&nbsp;
future product launches and events.

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:22.880
Through this entire branding process,&nbsp;
we’ve crafted our vision and strategy.&nbsp;

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:28.400
Our core mission is to bring joy to workspaces&nbsp;
and everyday experiences. Creating products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:35.360
that deserve to exist and carving out our "warm&nbsp;
tech" niche to stand apart from competitors. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:40.720
changes how we approach our products, as we take a&nbsp;
more curated approach in developing a thoughtfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:46.480
designed ecosystem of keyboards and accessories.
For marketing, we’ll emphasize transparency to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:51.120
connect with our audience by sharing more&nbsp;
of our story, behind-the-scenes content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:56.000
and introducing the team behind our brand.
One of the most valuable insights from our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:01.760
customer research: people connect with our brand&nbsp;
when they experience our keyboards firsthand. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:07.200
"aha moment" occurs when they see and type on&nbsp;
our products. That's why we plan to attend more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:12.960
in-person creative and tech events to create&nbsp;
meaningful connections and grow our community.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:17.360
With a strong brand and business&nbsp;
foundation in place, we're working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:23.440
on several exciting ongoing projects.
Our website redesign is complete. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:29.040
a massive change from where we were before, to&nbsp;
where we’re going as a brand. We’ve warmed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:34.800
the appearance of the site, simplified many of&nbsp;
the purchasing processes for customers like Jay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:40.240
and expanded areas that share more about our&nbsp;
brand for our curious customers like Tim.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:45.760
Development of the site is currently in progress&nbsp;
and will roll out slowly through the year. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:52.000
can follow our updates on modedesigns.com.
We're taking the first steps in developing more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:57.600
eco-friendly packaging, starting with our next&nbsp;
run of the Encore keyboard, releasing this summer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:04.240
We're moving away from foam inserts to recyclable&nbsp;
molded pulp and will feature our new brand look.&nbsp;

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:09.840
Xris and Andrew in Boston have built a new&nbsp;
studio setup to capture photos and videos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:14.000
which will be rolling out on&nbsp;
our site and in future content.&nbsp;

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:19.360
And the most exciting news: the next generation&nbsp;
of our products is taking shape. We’ve finished&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:24.640
most of the design of our next keyboard, and now&nbsp;
we’re working with engineers to complete a full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:30.400
overhaul of components to strengthen our position&nbsp;
as innovators in the mechanical keyboard space.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:35.040
We still have more work ahead, and it&nbsp;
will take time to see the impact of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:40.000
efforts. I plan to share updates about our&nbsp;
projects and processes on this channel. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:44.880
you’d like more content like this, let me know&nbsp;
in the comments and subscribe to follow along.&nbsp;

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:49.520
Ben Burns will also be creating content about&nbsp;
this project on his channel. Give him a follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:54.640
if you’d like more insights from his perspective.
Check the description for links to everything.&nbsp;

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:58.640
If you have any questions, ask,&nbsp;
and I'll do my best to answer them.&nbsp;

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:03.840
With that out of the way,&nbsp;
it's time to get back to work.

